# The app moved to its own origin. These five paths resolved on the apex until
# the split (the SPA fallback served the shell for anything), so bookmarks and
# any link already in the wild still point here. Send them across rather than
# letting them hit the 404 page.
/dashboard      https://app.heirlm.xyz/dashboard      301
/create-vault   https://app.heirlm.xyz/create-vault   301
/claim          https://app.heirlm.xyz/claim          301
/defer          https://app.heirlm.xyz/defer          301
/heartbeat      https://app.heirlm.xyz/heartbeat      301

# The old sitemap path. @astrojs/sitemap emits an index instead.
/sitemap.xml    /sitemap-index.xml                    301

# There is deliberately no rule for the old docs.heirlm.xyz here. Workers static
# assets only accept relative sources — an absolute one is rejected outright
# ("Only relative URLs are allowed", API code 100324) — and a relative `/*`
# would match this hostname too and swallow the whole site. A cross-hostname
# redirect has to be a Cloudflare Redirect Rule, configured on the zone.
#
# It is not worth one. The Mintlify site was never crawled (no Wayback
# snapshot), its DNS record is already deleted, and the hostname now resolves
# to nothing at all.
